@page "/docs/components/dialog"
@using Blaizio.Docs.Examples.Dialog
<PageTitle>Dialog - Blaizio</PageTitle>

<div class="typeset typeset-docs space-y-10">
    <header class="docs-page-header space-y-2.5">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Dialog</h1>
            <DocBadges Slug="dialog" />
        </div>
        <p>A modal layer with the expected behavior built in. Focus stays inside while it is open and returns to the trigger when it closes, the page behind stops scrolling, and Escape or a backdrop click dismisses it unless you turn that off.</p>
    </header>

    <UsageBlock Example="typeof(DialogUsageExample)"
                Description="After importing `Blaizio.Ui`, a trigger and a content block are all you need. Any action wrapped in `BzDialogClose` closes the dialog when clicked." />

    <CompositionTree Root="Anatomy"
                     Description="Every part of a dialog. The header holds the title and description, which also give the dialog its accessible name and description. Footer actions that should close it go inside `BzDialogClose`." />

    <ExamplesHeading />

    <Demo Title="Default"
          Description="The trigger and close parts render as a `BzButton` out of the box, so they accept `Variant` and `Size` directly."
          Example="typeof(DialogDefaultExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Custom trigger element (RenderAs)"
          Description="If the trigger should be a link, a card or one of your own components, use `RenderAs` and apply the attributes it provides to that element. It then opens the dialog and carries the right ARIA state."
          Example="typeof(DialogRenderAsTriggerExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Scrollable content" Example="typeof(DialogScrollableExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Sticky footer" Example="typeof(DialogStickyFooterExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Controlled" Description="Bind the open state to a field in your page when other code needs to open or close the dialog. In this example, every change shows a toast so you can follow it."
          Example="typeof(DialogControlledExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Nested dialogs"
          Description="A dialog can open another one. The inner dialog stacks on top, and when it closes, its result is passed back to the outer dialog."
          Example="typeof(DialogNestedExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Alert dialog inside"
          Description="To confirm a destructive action, open an `AlertDialog` from inside the dialog. It stacks above with its own backdrop. Cancel returns to the first dialog, and confirming closes both."
          Example="typeof(DialogAlertInsideExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Without close button" Example="typeof(DialogNoCloseExample)" />
    <Demo Title="Non-dismissible" Description="Set `PreventDismiss` when the user must make a choice. Escape and backdrop clicks are ignored and the corner close button is hidden, so only a `BzDialogClose` or your own code can close it." Example="typeof(DialogPreventDismissExample)" />
    <Demo Title="Customization"
          Description="Every part accepts `Class`, and the backdrop takes `OverlayClass`. This example uses them for a branded look with a custom radius, tinted surface and blurred backdrop."
          Example="typeof(DialogCustomExample)" />
    <Demo Title="RTL" Description="Inside a right-to-left `DirectionProvider`, the layout mirrors itself: text aligns to the right, the close button moves to the left corner and the footer buttons swap order."
          Example="typeof(DialogRtlExample)" />
</div>

@code {
    // The anatomy drawn by the Composition section - CompositionTree computes the connectors.
    private static readonly CompositionNode Anatomy = new("BzDialog",
        new CompositionNode("BzDialogTrigger"),
        new CompositionNode("BzDialogContent",
            new CompositionNode("BzDialogHeader",
                new CompositionNode("BzDialogTitle"),
                new CompositionNode("BzDialogDescription")),
            new CompositionNode("BzDialogFooter",
                new CompositionNode("BzDialogClose"))));
}
